From 8a3884235b3014c885343997b543af6d15b00d26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jules Drean <jules@tinfoil.sh>
Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 01:57:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 115/117] fix: sync stale GPU num_computed_tokens before MTP
 decode metadata kernel

Use seq_lens (GPU tensor) instead of CPU num_computed_tokens_cpu_tensor
to avoid CPU->GPU transfer that causes non-determinism with temperature=0.0.

Root cause: On the first MTP decode step after prefill, GPU
num_computed_tokens is stale (0 from prefill's copy_from_cpu). The
Triton kernel reads GPU and adds valid_count, producing wrong positions.

Fix: Derive correct value from seq_lens (GPU tensor holding
num_computed_tokens + num_scheduled_tokens from previous step).
GPU = seq_lens - valid_count, then kernel computes GPU + valid_count
= seq_lens_prev = correct new num_computed_tokens.

This is entirely GPU-side (copy_ + sub_ on default CUDA stream),
eliminating non-determinism from CPU->GPU timing perturbation.

A flag (_cc_mtp_decode_gpu_synced) ensures the sync only runs on the
first MTP step. The kernel maintains GPU correctly on subsequent steps.
The flag is reset when MTP fastpath disengages.

Verified: Gate 07 (DMF without BT dirty) passes 7/7 consistently across
3 runs. Gate 05/06 (with BT dirty) still has non-determinism from
VLLM_CC_BLOCK_TABLE_DIRTY_UPDATE, which is a separate issue.

Co-authored-by: factory-droid[bot] <138933559+factory-droid[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
